## BC-3 anti-facade verification

**NEGATIVE PATH (proven first):**
- MAPPING_INCOMPLETE when `severity` unfilled → rollback, zero m2 rows, zero status change
- MAPPING_INCOMPLETE when `clause_ref` unfilled → rollback
- MAPPING_INCOMPLETE when `corrective_action_desc` (action_desc) unfilled → rollback
- No audit event published on failure
- ZERO hardcoded defaults for clause_ref/severity/source/standard/nc_type under ANY code path

**POSITIVE PATH (single tenant transaction):**
1. Validate all maps_to_column required fields filled → else MAPPING_INCOMPLETE
2. Resolve clause_ref UUID → clause_no TEXT from qms.clause_registry (pending 011)
3. INSERT m2.nonconformities (standard, source, nc_type, description, clause_ref, severity, raised_by, created_by) — real 003 column names
4. INSERT m2.corrective_actions (nc_id::uuid from step 3, action_desc, owner_id, due_date::timestamptz, containment_flag, created_by) — real 003 column names
5. Stamp forms.records.m2_nc_id::uuid + status='complete' + completed_by + completed_at
6. Commit + publishAuditEvent (FormRecord.Submitted)

**m2.corrective_actions NOT NULL columns (required mapped):**
- action_desc ← corrective_action_desc (required, maps_to='action_desc')
- owner_id ← ca_owner (required, maps_to='owner_id')
- due_date ← ca_due_date (required, maps_to='due_date')

## reopenFormRecord (BC-5)

- Justification required (empty → JUSTIFICATION_REQUIRED)
- Only complete/approved can reopen (others → REOPEN_INVALID_STATUS)
- Status → 'reopened', clears completed_by/completed_at
- publishAuditEvent (FormRecord.Reopened) with justification in payload

